{"from": "claim:lk-22-04-06-money-agreed", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-15-thirty-silver", "note": "Luke agrees only that money was agreed to Judas; Matthew specifies thirty pieces of silver weighed out, and Luke adds the temple captains among those he talked with."}
{"from": "claim:lk-22-34-cockcrow-today", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-34-cockcrow-denial", "note": "Timing differs: Matthew puts the cockcrow before the three denials ('tonight, before the rooster crows'); Luke says the rooster will not crow 'today until you deny me three times'."}
{"from": "claim:lk-22-34-cockcrow-today", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mk-14-30-cockcrow-twice", "note": "Number differs: Mark has two cockcrows, the second before the third denial; Luke's prediction has one crow after all three denials, though Luke 22:61 recites 'before the rooster crows'."}
{"from": "claim:lk-22-17-18-cup-before-bread", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-22-19-20-bread-and-cup", "note": "Luke reports a cup before the bread (22:17-18) and another 'after supper' (22:20); Matthew 26:26-28 and Mark 14:22-24 report only the single cup with the bread."}
{"from": "claim:lk-22-39-mount-of-olives-custom", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-30-hymn-mount-olives", "note": "Luke omits the singing of the hymn and adds that going to the Mount of Olives was Jesus's custom; Matthew and Mark tie the Mount of Olives departure to the hymn."}
{"from": "claim:lk-22-51-healed-ear", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-51-sword-ear", "note": "Luke alone reports that Jesus touched the ear and healed it; he also says it was the right ear; Matthew and Mark report only the cutting off."}
{"from": "claim:lk-22-66-morning-council", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-59-council-death", "note": "Luke separates a morning assembly of the council from the arrest night; Matthew and Mark describe the council seeking testimony in a single night hearing."}
{"from": "claim:lk-22-69-son-of-man-right-hand", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-26-64-son-of-man-clouds", "note": "Luke's saying has the enthronement ('seated at the right hand of the power of God') but omits Matthew's 'coming on the clouds of the sky'."}
{"from": "artifact:codex-sinaiticus", "type": "preserves", "to": "passage:lk-22-43", "note": "Written by the original hand of Sinaiticus; the first corrector marked 22:43-44 for omission. Vaticanus omits the verses (see the passage variants)."}
{"from": "artifact:codex-sinaiticus", "type": "preserves", "to": "passage:lk-22-44", "note": "Written by the original hand of Sinaiticus; the first corrector marked 22:43-44 for omission. Vaticanus omits the verses (see the passage variants)."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-pesachim-10-7", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:sefaria-pesachim-10-7-third-cup", "note": "Reviewer 7: the third-cup quotation in the attests note was not in any source excerpt; this excerpt states it verbatim."}
{"from": "text:josephus-war-6-288-300", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-04-01-captain-of-the-temple", "grade": "A", "note": "Josephus (War 6.5.3, of the temple as it stood before 70 CE): the temple watchmen ran 'to the captain of the temple', who came up and shut the gate - the same temple-captain office (strategos tou hierou) Acts 4:1 names, acting in the temple; the same institution in the same place and period. Moved by reviewer 10 from the arrest claim, which the evidence does not attest (bundled-claim split, per the Acts 17 politarchs model)."}
{"from": "text:josephus-war-6-288-300", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-22-52-captains-arrest", "grade": "B", "note": "Confirms the institutional setting of the arresting party: the temple watch and its captain, with the chief priests and elders, stood in Jerusalem in the same period; it does not attest that they came against Jesus. Regraded A to B when the office claim merged into claim:ac-04-01-captain-of-the-temple per the architect's titles-and-offices ruling (2026-11-15)."}
{"from": "passage:lk-22-52", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:ac-04-01-captain-of-the-temple"}
